{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now","id":710646,"title":"Beast: The Primordial backer PDF errata thread [it's out now]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-20T08:42:40-07:00","id":710646,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Beast: The Primordial backer PDF errata thread [it's out now]","content":"EDIT: The advance PDF for backers is out now! If you find any typos or visual glitches, please report them here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 10-28-2015, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T14:40:50-07:00","id":735872,"title":"","content":"&quot;Isolde produces a little black vile&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 9. Should be &quot;vial.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8945-the-wyzard","name":"The Wyzard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8945_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T14:52:33-07:00","id":735917,"title":"","content":"References to the <b>Homecoming</b> on p.79-80 and the Chart Quick Reference on p.337, which should probably be replaced with <b>Devouring</b> in accordance with the change in terminology.<br /> <br /> p.20-1: &quot;The three Inheritance states are Incarnate, Unfettered, and <b>Rampant.</b>&quot; &quot;Merger: The process by which the Beast joins with her Horror, creating a near-mindless monster unable to access the Primordial Dream, thus achieving the <b>Unleashed</b> Inheritance.&quot; &quot;<b>Unleashed</b> Inheritance: The Inheritance gained when a Beast undergoes Merger.&quot; All references outside the Lexicon refer to the physical-world Inheritance as &quot;Rampant,&quot; but this is also the name given to the Lucifuge-analogues in the Tokyo setting. Needs disentangling.<br /> <br /> p.47: &quot;Beyond the fence, <b>though</b> darkness not even Tanya\u2019s keen eyes could pierce, there was something waiting.&quot; Should be &quot;through&quot;.<br /> <br /> p.97: &quot;Opening a Pathway to the exact location from which the Beast created a Chamber is easiest, but <b>desperate Beasts and cunning would-be intruders can use similar locations by spending a point of Willpower during the attempt and incurring an additional dice penalty</b> based on how well the location matches.&quot; Phrasing suggests this is an additional cost, but subsequent roll description includes &quot;Cost: 1 Willpower&quot; as though this is a baseline facet of opening a Primordial Pathway anywhere. Suggest removing the Cost line or the &quot;by spending a point of Willpower during the attempt&quot; if opening a Pathway without an Exact similarity is not meant to cost 2 Willpower.<br /> <br /> p.99: &quot;<b>Visitors or intruders using Primordial Pathways from anything other than the Primordial Dream are physically present</b>, while characters whose nightmares touch the Primordial Dream (Beasts who have yet to undergo the Devouring, for example) are present in a dream state.&quot; Should probably be &quot;anything other than the Astral [Realms],&quot; else this is a severe and bizarre complication for, say, mages engaging in highly inadvisable meditation.<br /> <br /> p162. &quot;If using Social maneuvering on a character that doesn\u2019t have a Vice (like a vampire or a Beast), a temptation that plays to <b>a similar trait, like Life or Mask,</b> can have the same effect at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.&quot; Per Second Edition Vampire, the Kindred substitute for Vice is Dirge, not Mask; analogously, it is possible that the Vice-equivalent for Beasts should be Legend rather than Life.<br /> <br /> p.227: &quot;The curse of the Created, however, is in humanity\u2019s reaction to them. Prometheans who stay in one place for too long and use their alchemical powers too much engender \u201cDisquiet,\u201d <b>which to Beasts all-too-closely resembles the creation of Heroes.</b>&quot; References the pre-revision version of how Heroes worked, should probably be altered or removed.<br /> <br /> p.236: &quot;<b>Lurkers</b> who Hunger to hoard knowledge find this ability useful for information gathering.&quot; &quot;Some <b>Lurkers</b> have managed to find ways \u2014 either through the Dream, or in the physical realm \u2014 to enter these realms, exploring them for their own reasons.&quot; Obsolete terminology that now solely refers to the Eshmaki. Suggest replacing with &quot;Unfettered.&quot;<br /> <br /> p.249: &quot;I feel larger, fuller, and <b>so much than</b> the skin, muscle, and bone that contains me.&quot; Should probably be &quot;so much more than&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-04-2015, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T14:56:40-07:00","id":735926,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Opening of Pg. 285-&quot;the presentation on p. XX, that identifies Heroes as reactive; both at true.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Replace &quot;at&quot; with &quot;are&quot;<br /> <br /> Forging a Hero, pg. 271\u200f<br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Book says &quot;Any time a Beast commits an action </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">that could result in a Hero\u2019s creation, it happens.&quot;</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Should probably relate it to anything that activates Hero Tracking.</span></span></span><br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:00:49-07:00","id":735935,"title":"","content":"Opening fiction, fifth paragraph:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ben was often got in moods where only Laurie could console him. </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> There's a stray word in there. It works as &quot;Ben often got in moods&quot; or &quot;Ben was often in moods&quot;, but &quot;was often got&quot; doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:01:02-07:00","id":735936,"title":"","content":"&quot;Her nightmares are made all the worse because she is more often than the predator than the prey.&quot; Pg. 14. One of the two &quot;than&quot; needs to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8945-the-wyzard","name":"The Wyzard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8945_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:12:00-07:00","id":735949,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Still on the opening fiction:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:VintageTypewriter-Corona\"><span style=\"font-family:VintageTypewriter-Corona\">She\u2019d been forced to swap with Jess and sit </span></span><span style=\"font-family:VintageTypewriter-Corona\"><span style=\"font-family:VintageTypewriter-Corona\">in the backseat with him to quiet him down on the drive from Philadelphia, and </span></span><span style=\"font-family:VintageTypewriter-Corona\"><span style=\"font-family:VintageTypewriter-Corona\">even then he\u2019d been so unruly that Matt had joked about leaving him to be raised </span></span><span style=\"font-family:VintageTypewriter-Corona\"><span style=\"font-family:VintageTypewriter-Corona\">by coyotes in the Pine Barrens.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:VintageTypewriter-Corona\"><span style=\"font-family:VintageTypewriter-Corona\">This may be nitpicky, but that's really a mouthful. I'd be sorely tempted to add a comma after &quot;swap with Jess&quot;, and to break it into two sentences, <i>a la</i>:<br /> <br /> &quot;She'd been forced to swap with Jess, and sit in the backseat to quiet him down on the drive from Philadelphia. Even then, he'd been so unruly that Matt had joked about leaving him to be raised by coyotes in the Pine Barrens.&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 10-28-2015, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:30:50-07:00","id":736000,"title":"","content":"Noticed one pretty quickly on the cover:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast: The Primordial Cover</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Storytell<i><b>er</b></i> Game of Endless Appetite</div> </div> </div> </div>That should be Storytell<i><b>ing</b></i>, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:51:53-07:00","id":736053,"title":"","content":"I'm seeing some punctuation issues in &quot;Tales of the Dark Mother: Sabia&quot;. For example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sabia falls in an ugly, graceless kind of way as Isolde, the Hero wrenches the sword back. </div> </div> </div>Need a comma after &quot;the Hero&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She\u2019s six-years-old with sleep paralysis, being weighed down by a nothing in the dark, calling out without a word for her mother to Please help! Please help! </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't there be quote marks around &quot;Please help!&quot;? I'd also be tempted to cut &quot;being&quot;, and capitalize &quot;nothing&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you want to go back to sleep, baby?<br /> <br /> &quot;I\u2019m scared.&quot;<br /> <br /> Do you want to stay up with me?<br /> <br /> &quot;I don\u2019t know.&quot;<br /> <br /> Her mother kisses her forehead and sings a lullaby she doesn\u2019t remember. It has no notes. It\u2019s the color of ice and sweet like corpses. It\u2019s the most wonderful thing Sabia has ever felt. It makes her think of pain. Of the nothing in the dark. That fear is her friend.<br /> <br /> Do you want to go back to sleep? </div> </div> </div>Like the imagery, but I'm tempted to play with the font of the mother's lines. In this situation, it makes sense not to use quote marks (after all, who says the Dark Mother &quot;speaks&quot; as humans understand the concept?) However, it might be worth experimenting with various font tricks to set her words off - italicizing or bolding her lines, or doing them in a visibly different font . . . Something to put that special emphasis on them, and show the omission of standard quote marks is deliberate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 10-28-2015, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T16:14:07-07:00","id":736122,"title":"","content":"Page fourteen (Introduction):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Her nightmares are made all the worse because she is more often <b>than</b> the predator than the prey. </div> </div> </div>I think you either have an extra &quot;than&quot; there, or lost a &quot;not&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T16:27:19-07:00","id":736143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=735917#post735917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p.47: &quot;Beyond the fence, <b>though</b> darkness not even Tanya\u2019s keen eyes could pierce, there was something waiting.&quot; Should be &quot;though&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that &quot;though&quot; should be &quot;th<u>r</u>ough.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/201-jadasc","name":"Jadasc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T16:29:54-07:00","id":736152,"title":"","content":"Page Fifteen:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All Beasts have a primal drive called Hunger, which they must indulge to sate the appetite of the Horror. </div> </div> </div>Picking nits again - but this seems awkwardly worded. Doesn't ever living thing have a primal drive to eat? Known as &quot;hunger&quot;? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However it is interpreted, Hunger must always feed the Horror\u2019s appetite. </div> </div> </div>Again, seems awkward and redundant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Put another way, as older Beasts sometimes tell younger ones, &quot;if someone eats, something else gets eaten.&quot; A Beast may console herself by thinking that she only hurts &quot;bad people&quot; to sate her Hunger (either to scare the subject straight or make an example of him), for example, but deep down she knows that as far as her Horror is concerned, really anyone would do \u2014 and one day, if she isn\u2019t careful, they just might </div> </div> </div>I suggest flipping this around a bit. The line about &quot;if someone eats, something gets eaten&quot; makes a <i>lot</i> more sense after hearing some of the justifications younger Beasts use.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T16:42:52-07:00","id":736229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is the modern world so different? Death still comes suddenly<br /> and violently, now at the hands of strangers now instead<br /> of animals. </div> </div> </div>Pg. 55, extra &quot;now.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8945-the-wyzard","name":"The Wyzard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8945_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T17:14:46-07:00","id":736327,"title":"","content":"Bottom of p. 54, in the<i> View from Without </i>sidebar,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I saw her surrounded by men. The men carried bats and boards and knives, and I <b>though</b>, for a moment, she\u2019s like me. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Though&quot; should be &quot;thought.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:41:53-07:00","id":736473,"title":"","content":"On p.2 of the four-page character sheet, &quot;Breaking Points&quot; appears as a category header, but the Children don't have those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:45:04-07:00","id":736475,"title":"","content":"<b>Family and Hunger</b><br /> <br /> Are you sure you want to lay it out this way? A brief intro to <i>both</i> Family and Hunger at the very beginning, and that's it? With no transition in between Family and Hunger?<br /> <br /> Also, the italicized intro paragraph for each Family (visually) blends right into the description of the Family. I like the intros . . .but they needs something more to set them off from the general text<br /> <br /> <u><i>Anakim</i></u><br /> p. 26<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When she freed the terrors of the world from their secret hiding place and held back hope from the world, </div> </div> </div> Shouldn\u2019t that be &quot;secret hiding <i>places</i><b>&quot; </b>(plural)? And where does holding back hope come from? Seems like a mangled mix of Pandora's Box, and the richest man in the world (whom Raven stole the sun &amp; stars from)<br /> <br /> Not sure about the choice of mythical giant families. <i>Three</i> out of the four are European . . . but no mention of the Hekatonkheires (Hundred Handed Ones), arguably the greatest giants in mythology? Briareus - all by his lonesome self - smacked down the entire Greek pantheon, when the Olympians dared challenge Zeus<br /> <br /> P. 27<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The dreamer is left with no doubt that might makes right, and that the Giant has all the right in the world. </div> </div> </div>Shouldn\u2019t that be &quot;the Giant has all the <b>m</b>ight in the world&quot;?<br /> <br /> <u><i>Hungers</i></u><br /> <br /> p. 36<br /> Last line references &quot;Soul&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An Eshmaki Tyrant\u2019s Soul hunts from the shadows, its form never fully seen; the glimpses that his victims catch reveal </div> </div> </div>p.37<br /> Again, a reference to &quot;Soul&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An Ugallu Tyrant\u2019s Soul often appears impressive in his own right, </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 10-28-2015, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:54:32-07:00","id":736491,"title":"","content":"p.19: Disney's <i>Beauty &amp; the Beast</i> is from 1991, not 1997.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T19:06:56-07:00","id":736506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=736475#post736475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> P. 27<br /> Shouldn\u2019t that be &quot;the Giant has all the <b>m</b>ight in the world&quot;?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly sure that one's correct, but that's Rose's work, so I can't say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T19:07:53-07:00","id":736509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=736000#post736000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noticed one pretty quickly on the cover:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That should be Storytell<i><b>ing</b></i>, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the first thing I noticed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.j