"content":"pg 59, section on Changelings<br /> This bit plays up the idea of Changelings having been <i>made</i> vs Beasts having been <i>born</i>. With Beasts now having originally just been otherwise ordinary humans with stronger dreaming connections to the Primordial Dream than was usual who had to be made into Beasts by the Devouring, this distinction no longer seems valid. Both Beasts and Changelings are now <i>made</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T13:47:49-07:00","id":742709,"title":"","content":"pg 234.<br /> &quot;The first path is known as the Retreat, and occurs when the Beast while separated from her soul.&quot;<br /> <br /> When the beast while separated from her soul? There's a verb missing here. Unless it only happens if you accidentally the whole Inheritance, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T16:14:30-07:00","id":743184,"title":"","content":"pg. 117: Iron Skin, is the prerequisite and cost supposed to have been changed? Are updates to general merits in this book supposed to be official errata to base rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9010-umbravenatir","name":"umbravenatir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T04:34:23-07:00","id":744210,"title":"","content":"P 41 ...fearsome creatures see them nothing more than the next meal. Should probably be ...fearsome creatures see them <b>as</b> nothing more than the next meal.<br /> <br /> P. 42 ...zir assigned gender. Should probably be zir<b>'s</b> assigned gender.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 10-31-2015, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T07:39:43-07:00","id":744449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=744210#post744210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P 41 ...fearsome creatures see them nothing more than the next meal. Should probably be ...fearsome creatures see them <b>as</b> nothing more than the next meal.<br /> <br /> P. 42 ...zir assigned gender. Should probably be zir<b>'s</b> assigned gender.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually argue that they should change &quot;They don't know zir's real name....&quot; to &quot;They don't know zir real name...&quot; and leave &quot;zir assigned gender&quot; as-is. &quot;Zir&quot; seems to take the place of his/her, which you would use as &quot;his/her real name or his/her assigned gender.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T12:24:33-07:00","id":744830,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">p. 41, second column: &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\">Some leave a single sting, <span style=\"color:#000000\">something that itches and aches but causes no las<u>t</u><b><u>ing</u> </b>harm.</span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> p. 56, in the second paragraph of the View from Without: &quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">One of them was a big, brutish guy name<u><b>d</b></u> Zane.</span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">&quot;</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9032,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9032-lurkbeast","user":"LurkBeast","date":". 10-31-2015, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9032-lurkbeast","name":"LurkBeast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9032_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:11:33-07:00","id":745352,"title":"","content":"pg. 68<br /> &quot;That by itself is understandable. The problem is that<br /> Heroes aren\u2019t really doing it because they want to put down a<br /> monster. Heroes feel that they should loom large over humanity\u2019s<br /> dreams. People shouldn\u2019t be having nightmares of monsters,<br /> but dreaming of feverish adulation. They Hero longs to<br /> enter a Beast\u2019s Lair, cut out its Horror\u2019s heart, and substitute<br /> his smiling, bloodied face in the dreams of all whom the Beast<br /> would have victimized.<br /> <br /> Entering a Beast\u2019s Lair isn\u2019t always possible, though. Doing<br /> so is difficult and dangerous. Finding a Beast in the waking world<br /> is easier; killing her there, though difficult, is much simpler to<br /> accomplish. Heroes might dream of grand climactic battles in<br /> the Lair, but when push comes to shove, they\u2019ll settle for a shotgun<br /> blast or an IED in the Beast\u2019s doorway. Despite the Hero\u2019s<br /> grandiose dreams, what he really wants is to see the Beast dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> ... So &quot;Heroes aren't doing it because they want to put down a monster,&quot; but &quot;Despite the Hero's grandiose dreams, what he really wants is to see the beast dead&quot;? This could use some revision.<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T22:53:45-07:00","id":745874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=745352#post745352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">pg. 68<br /> &quot;That by itself is understandable. The problem is that<br /> Heroes aren\u2019t really doing it because they want to put down a<br /> monster. Heroes feel that they should loom large over humanity\u2019s<br /> dreams. People shouldn\u2019t be having nightmares of monsters,<br /> but dreaming of feverish adulation. They Hero longs to<br /> enter a Beast\u2019s Lair, cut out its Horror\u2019s heart, and substitute<br /> his smiling, bloodied face in the dreams of all whom the Beast<br /> would have victimized.<br /> <br /> Entering a Beast\u2019s Lair isn\u2019t always possible, though. Doing<br /> so is difficult and dangerous. Finding a Beast in the waking world<br /> is easier; killing her there, though difficult, is much simpler to<br /> accomplish. Heroes might dream of grand climactic battles in<br /> the Lair, but when push comes to shove, they\u2019ll settle for a shotgun<br /> blast or an IED in the Beast\u2019s doorway. Despite the Hero\u2019s<br /> grandiose dreams, what he really wants is to see the Beast dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> ... So &quot;Heroes aren't doing it because they want to put down a monster,&quot; but &quot;Despite the Hero's grandiose dreams, what he really wants is to see the beast dead&quot;? This could use some revision.<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps replace the word &quot;dreams,&quot; in the last line of text with, &quot;delusions.&quot; I'd argue that the dissonance between the two paragraphs is intentional, in order to sell that the Heroes aren't operating in an internally consistent narrative, and that the rationalizations an NPC Hero might try to sell the players wouldn't generally reflect the actual Maslowean conflict at play within the Heroic Psyche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T00:27:53-07:00","id":746031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=745874#post745874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps replace the word &quot;dreams,&quot; in the last line of text with, &quot;delusions.&quot; I'd argue that the dissonance between the two paragraphs is intentional, in order to sell that the Heroes aren't operating in an internally consistent narrative, and that the rationalizations an NPC Hero might try to sell the players wouldn't generally reflect the actual Maslowean conflict at play within the Heroic Psyche.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While that could be very effective in a story that focused on a Hero and served to underline their internally inconsistent and cognitively dissonant operations, it is suboptimal in the section that is supposed to describe heroes to the players and the GM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T00:54:38-07:00","id":746046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=746031#post746031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While that could be very effective in a story that focused on a Hero and served to underline their internally inconsistent and cognitively dissonant operations, it is suboptimal in the section that is supposed to describe heroes to the players and the GM.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't disagree that it's something of a tangle, it's still pretty clear that &quot;the Hero wants the unconscious accolades associated with killing a Beast and he's not all that fussed about how they're accomplished or why&quot; is the combined meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T07:38:11-08:00","id":746580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=742323#post742323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">pg 59, section on Changelings<br /> This bit plays up the idea of Changelings having been <i>made</i> vs Beasts having been <i>born</i>. With Beasts now having originally just been otherwise ordinary humans with stronger dreaming connections to the Primordial Dream than was usual who had to be made into Beasts by the Devouring, this distinction no longer seems valid. Both Beasts and Changelings are now <i>made</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between having your human self altered by exposure to the stuff of living narrative and fantastical otherness and torn off bits of your soul filled in by the substance of that same realm; and coming into your true monstrous self after the thin semblance of human soul-stuff keeping you from actualization has been eroded and devoured by repeated nightmares, a process facilitated by the intervention of an already realized family member of your astral lineage of fear.<br /> <br /> No matter what the introduction of the book has to say about it, that section is not innacurate about the differences between Beasts and Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T00:36:36-08:00","id":748616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=746580#post746580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a difference between having your human self altered by exposure to the stuff of living narrative and fantastical otherness and torn off bits of your soul filled in by the substance of that same realm; and coming into your true monstrous self after the thin semblance of human soul-stuff keeping you from actualization has been eroded and devoured by repeated nightmares, a process facilitated by the intervention of an already realized family member of your astral lineage of fear.<br /> <br /> No matter what the introduction of the book has to say about it, that section is not innacurate about the differences between Beasts and Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For my part, I think it's actually very problematic if the book's introduction doesn't reflect the intent of the rest of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6806-abattoirista","name":"Abattoirista","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T04:14:13-08:00","id":748858,"title":"","content":"It definitely is, yes. The introduction in the PDF right now is outdated and doesn't accurately reflect important details as they are given and developed on the rest of the text, IMO.<br /> <br /> It looks like the same kind of mistake as Chapter 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T15:47:59-08:00","id":750232,"title":"","content":"P. 55. Under Makara: ...water as the bringer and sustained of life. Should be ...water as the bringer and sustaine<b>r</b> of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 11-03-2015, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T16:21:52-08:00","id":750253,"title":"","content":"Pg. 180<br /> <br /> The entry for Stun Gun mentions three intensities, but only says that they correspond to the availabilities. There's no description of the effect of these intensities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4725-murder_of_craws","name":"Murder_of_Craws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4725_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T18:39:09-08:00","id":750396,"title":"","content":"On page 102, the text for Currents implies that the Beast gets to choose the Strength rating every time the Lair Trait is manifested; I'm fairly certain that's meant to be set when the Lair Trait is acquired originally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T21:57:25-08:00","id":753029,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Introduction:</b></u><br /> <br /> On pages eleven and twelve, fourteen and fifteen . . . Clearly &quot;Devouring&quot; &amp; &quot;Horror&quot; have won out, over &quot;Homecoming&quot; and &quot;Soul&quot;. It shifts some interpretations, but I think most of us can live with that. However, whomever did the re-writes in this section is pushing a radically different vision of Beasts. They're basically describing Beasts as proto-Dreamspeakers who sold their souls (and any chance of Awakening) in exchange for getting rid of the visions &amp; nightmares, plus the power of a Horror.<br /> <br /> Coupled with a Beast's need to feed their Hunger. . . That pretty much changes Beasts into psychic vampires. Ones who sold out to the darkness, and agreed to prey on their former species. And frankly, that makes them bad guys. Not shades of grey - just outright traitors and monsters. If this view sticks, Heroes are right to pursue and kill Beasts.<br /> <br /> So its a very problematic reinterpretation - one that, frankly, the other chapters don't support at all. Heck, even the Q&amp;A box on page 12<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Beasts aren\u2019t human:</b> True. Beasts are born human, though most of them experience deep, primal nightmares throughout their lives \u2014 an intrinsic connection to the Primordial Dream. At some point, another of the Children finds the incipient Beast and offers to change her through Devouring. From that point on, the person is no longer fully human, having lost her soul and replaced it with a Horror.<br /> <br /> Some Beasts claim that they have never been human, however, and that the Devouring merely cleared away detritus. Instead of replacing a human soul with a Horror, they say, the Devouring clarifies the connection, allowing the Horror that was always present to come forth. Indeed, some Beasts claim that the Devouring was spontaneous and that no other Beast was involved. In either case, whether another Beast instigated the Devouring or it happened on its own \u2014 whether a Beast was human or just believed she was \u2014 the Children are not human. </div> </div> </div>Which points out - at the very beginning - that Beast aren't human. This new introduction provides no support <i>whatsoever </i>for the second type of Beast (never human, or self-Devoured) . . . and that's really the kind that sold most people on <i>Beast</i>. Simultaneously being a primal fear coping with the fact they have &quot;friends&quot; and &quot;family&quot; now, <i>and</i> a person who finds out the reason the never fit in with other humans, is because they <i>weren't</i> human?<br /> <br /> And, frankly, wouldn't it be more fun to spend some of that word count on talking about how, while feeding on humans, a Beast will sometimes find one who's NOT PREY. How, when they try to feed on the person, a gigantic hand slaps them away or tentacles wrap possessively around their attempted meal (in the Dream, of course)? How, when they gaze into the NOT PREY's eyes, they see the same darkness from which they were born?<br /> <br /> Plus, the interpretation being pushed by this intro raises other problems. Maybe its addressed later in the book (still working on the second half), but what stops a Beast from randomly devouring people's souls, allowing a Horror to forcibly claim the person? Or why don't Horrors start bonding with other people who've been de-souled by other means?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Hmm . . . on a related note, would it be possible to add &quot;Homecoming&quot; to the vocabulary list on page 19 &amp; 20? There seems to be enough white space to accommodate it. Plus, it makes sense that the never-humans and self-devoured would have their own term for what happens to them when they come into their nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 11-04-2015, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T22:55:25-08:00","id":753084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=753029#post753029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On pages eleven and twelve, fourteen and fifteen . . . Clearly &quot;Devouring&quot; &amp; &quot;Horror&quot; have won out, over &quot;Homecoming&quot; and &quot;Soul&quot;. It shifts some interpretations, but I think most of us can live with that. However, whomever did the re-writes in this section is pushing a radically different vision of Beasts. They're basically describing Beasts as proto-Dreamspeakers who sold their souls (and any chance of Awakening) in exchange for getting rid of the visions &amp; nightmares, plus the power of a Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/582155-beast-changes\">Wrong thread</a>, Vorlon, unless you have incredibly solid evidence for any of this being a typo or visual glitch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-04-2015, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T22:56:59-08:00","id":753085,"title":"","content":"Page 51<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Horror is a nightmare monster, a creature from the dreams of a terrified human being. Modern Beasts theorize that every time a person dreams of monsters, that monster either already exists somewhere in the Primordial Dream (and the dream calls on ancestral memory) or is created at that moment as a Horror (if the dreamer is one of the special few whose dreams go so deep). In any case, the Horror drifts through the Dream, eventually reaching one of the outer Chambers. If it finds one it considers habitable, it enters it, settles down, and bonds with it. The Chamber becomes a Lair. </div> </div> </div>The second to last line feels awkward. At the very least, it contains excess &quot;it&quot;s. Even a slight tweak would help, something like:<br /> <br /> &quot;If it finds one it considers habitable, it enters, settles down, and bonds with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Horrors, on their own, rarely touch the minds of human beings deeply enough to have a greater effect than a particularly intense nightmare; it might be a cause for discussion, even analysis, but doesn\u2019t do any lasting harm to a person. Only when Lairs are close to the waking world do the nightmares have the power to cause real harm. The primary way this happens, of course, is when a human being becomes a Beast. </div> </div> </div>Kind of a run-on. Consider re-editing, maybe along the lines of:<br /> <br /> &quot;On their own, Horrors rarely cause anything more than a particularly intense nightmare. One that might be cause for discussion, even analysis, but without inflicting any lasting harm. Only when a Lair drifts close to the waking world does a Horror gain the power to cause real harm. And nothing draws a Lair closer than the birth of a Beast . . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Growing up estranged or even bullied, the dreamer has every reason to hate her tormentors, but does that make the human race her enemy? What about her family? That one teacher who spoke up for her? The boy next door who had a crush on her even though she was &quot;weird?&quot; <b>These people whom she recognizes as people and who recognize her in turn, these are family even if they aren\u2019t kin.</b> Is she, then, really a part of this community? If so, then why can\u2019t the rest of them recognize it? </div> </div> </div>There's a typo here. Either it should be &quot;Those people whom&quot; or &quot;These are people whom&quot;. Also might want to consider adding a comma after &quot;as people&quot;, and breaking the sentence in two (with a period after &quot;in turn&quot;).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=753029#post753029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Introduction:</b></u><br /> <br /> On pages eleven and twelve, fourteen and fifteen . . . Clearly &quot;Devouring&quot; &amp; &quot;Horror&quot; have won out, over &quot;Homecoming&quot; and &quot;Soul&quot;. It shifts some interpretations, but I think most of us can live with that. However, whomever did the re-writes in this section is pushing a radically different vision of Beasts. They're basically describing Beasts as proto-Dreamspeakers who sold their souls (and any chance of Awakening) in exchange for getting rid of the visions &amp; nightmares, plus the power of a Horror. . .<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oops - missed the earlier post about this being an old draft. Still would like to see &quot;Homecoming&quot; added to the vocab list. <br /> <br /> Will there be a re-release of the pdf? Kind of hard to proof chapters we can't see.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T23:38:21-08:00","id":753118,"title":"","content":"Really, really liking the art. Kudos both to the artists, and whomever hired them.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 53</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Beast looks at the world through her Horror\u2019s eyes. To others, an Eshmaki is just a sleek young woman with sun-darkened skin and the kind of lean muscle that does not come from a gym. Her true self may be a serpentine dragon, but she is confined by the physical reality of her human self, at least in the waking world. </div> </div> </div>Although I like the first line, it doesn't really seem to fit the rest of the paragraph.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aspects of her Lair bleed into the environment as the Beast concentrates. Heat shimmer fills the air. The sky grows sullen with the glow of distant fires and ash blows on the wind like snow. Shifting her perceptions only takes a modicum of effort, but seeing truly is harder when Hunger gnaws at her.<br /> <br /> The Beast can draw upon her Horror and aspects of her Lair \u2014 its heat, its darkness \u2014 to perform supernatural feats in the waking world known as Atavisms. These powers become more potent in locations that echo her Lair in some way, consciously infecting those around her with her fear. When a Beast uses an Atavism, any nearby being with supernatural awareness \u2014 be it one of the Beast\u2019s inhuman cousins like a vampire, or simply a mortal with some psychic affinity \u2014 catches a clear glimpse of the Horror in all its monstrous glory. </div> </div> </div>The first line of the second paragraph seems extraneous - just repeating information from the first one.<br /> <br /> And getting a little nitpicky:<br /> <br /> * The first line of the first paragraph is fine as is. But consider adding a bit of flair. For example, perhaps instead of &quot;as the Beast concentrates&quot;, how about something like &quot;when the Beast calls&quot; or 'when the Horror stirs&quot;?<br /> <br /> * Like &quot;consciously infecting&quot; (nice imagery there), but that sentence could be a bit neater, and it kind of makes it sound like the Beast herself is afraid.<br /> <br /> * Not wild &quot;any nearby being&quot; - even &quot;any being nearby&quot; is better<br /> <br /> <b>p. 54 </b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THE VIEW FROM WITHOUT:<br /> JULIA PHOENIX, GALATEID<br /> I saw her surrounded by men. The men carried bats and boards and knives, and I though, for a moment, she\u2019s like me. They hate her so. But I did not feel her inner fire, and I thought that something was happening that I did not understand. So I watched, but I promised myself if the men started to hurt her, I would intervene. </div> </div> </div>Not wild about &quot;men. The men carried&quot;. I\u2019d suggest something more like<br /> &quot;I saw her surround by men. Men who carried bats and boards and knives&quot;<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also a missing &quot;t&quot; in &quot;thought&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She fought them. She threw one against a wall so hard he bled. She punched one in the chest and he dropped, coughing, spitting red. But then one moved in behind her with a knife and I yelled a warning. The woman turned and exhaled fire. And I saw \u2014 I promise, I saw \u2014 the dragon, superimposed on her, mighty and terrible and resplendent and beautiful. The man ran, burning, only to collapse. The other men stood and staggered away. </div> </div> </div>Are you sure you want to start three sentences in a row with &quot;She&quot;?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I climbed down from the fire escape into the alley. I did not know what to say to her, this beauty, this woman with a dragon in her. I could not feel her inner fire the way I would with another like me, but I had, beyond doubt, seen it. </div> </div> </div>Possible typo - shouldn\u2019t it be &quot;beyond <b>a</b> doubt&quot;?<br /> <br /> <b>p.56</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sometimes that means tough love, of course; a Beast who can\u2019t or won\u2019t curb her predatory impulses attracts attention from Heroes or extended family, and that endangers all of the Children. </div> </div> </div>I recommend tweaking this sentence, and (definitely) breaking it into two. Something like:<br /> <br /> &quot;Sometimes that meant tough love, of course. A Beast who can't (or won't) curb her predatory impulses attracts attention from Heroes or extended family, and that endangers everyone.&quot;<br /> <br /> And this might be nitpicky, but:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts sense each other in a general way. They instinctively know someone is in their city and will eventually cross paths in the Primordial Dream. </div> </div> </div>I'd be tempted to italicize &quot;their&quot;, to emphasize that the Beast considers that city as their private hunting grounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 11-04-2015, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T00:05:43-08:00","id":753167,"title":"","content":"Like the tone of the werewolf sidebar. The image of a hungry werewolf, having a bad day, deciding to eat some people . . .and then walking away when a Beast shows, terrified of what he might become, if he joined her. . .<br /> <br /> <b>p. 64</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Teaching Through Fear&quot; sidebar<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Make no mistake, not all Beasts are good teachers. Some make weak stabs <b>are</b> teaching but really . . . </div> </div> </div>Apparent typo - I'm guessing that's supposed to be an &quot;at&quot;, not an &quot;are&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Teaching a lesson through terror is morally reprehensible to most people\u2026 </div> </div> </div>Since when? The notion of the &quot;burned hand teaches best&quot; is a classic conceit, and shows up in everything from raising kids to the &quot;deterrence&quot; theory of incarceration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Beasts are honest, they admit they use the concept of &quot;lessons&quot; to make what they do more palatable. Some Beasts rail at that notion, claiming divine purpose. Others try to make the lessons matter and improve humanity \u2014 whether the Dark Mother charges them with it or not, it\u2019s a noble pursuit. Still others shrug, cast off even the idea of a higher calling, and just feast. </div> </div> </div>First line is way too strong, which brings it into direct conflict with every line after it (in that paragraph). I think you want to stick a &quot;most&quot; or &quot;many&quot; in there, something like:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>many</b> admit they use the concept&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T00:59:17-08:00","id":753354,"title":"","content":"On page 248, &quot;Hero&quot;, where Ryan attacks Ben, the female vampire's name changes. Previously its always been &quot;Noelle&quot;, but here she's referred to (repeatedly) as &quot;Noel&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T02:07:15-08:00","id":753448,"title":"","content":"p.28 - Eshmaki Family general description:<br /> <br /> &quot;When the Dark Mother gave birth to your kind as She Who Lives in Her Shadow, she did so in the dark. Some other Children think it was out of shame, but you know better. You know she was giving you life <b>in your natural element</b>, birthing and leaving your ancestors <b>in their natural element</b>, so that they might understand loneliness but never fear being alone. &quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Natural element</b> is unneeded repetition here, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-04-2015, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T05:00:32-08:00","id":753713,"title":"","content":"On page 79 under the Legend and Life section you state &quot;You can find more information on Legend and Life on p. 87.&quot; While there is info on Life and legend on page 87, page 85 is where the info actually begins, and most of the Life and Legend info is on page 86.<br /> <br /> Continuing on page 79, there is no link/reference to what page you can find nightmares on, although you do have one for Atavisms ( &quot;You can find more on Atavisms on p. 121&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9094-kilnard","user":"Kilnard","date":". 11-04-2015, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9094-kilnard","name":"Kilnard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T07:47:09-08:00","id":753998,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this is actually a problem, but one of the new &quot;Tales of the Dark Mother&quot; vignettes contradicts the section on Hunter/Beast crossovers (specifically the part in the latter about Cheiron agents' not being kin).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T07:48:21-08:00","id":754000,"title":"","content":"The Patient Merit on page 118 stills says (p. XX) instead of a page number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9094-kilnard","name":"Kilnard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:27:58-08:00","id":754209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=753354#post753354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On page 248, &quot;Hero&quot;, where Ryan attacks Ben, the female vampire's name changes. Previously its always been &quot;Noelle&quot;, but here she's referred to (repeatedly) as &quot;Noel&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Noel/le is genderfluid (hence &quot;femme presentation&quot; in &quot;Kinship&quot; on p.146 and the use of &quot;he&quot; pronouns for Noel in Hero).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T18:33:15-08:00","id":755535,"title":"","content":"P. 72, just after the italicized section in column 2. &quot;Forget his delusions...the monsters in the deep that his mistook...&quot;<br /> <br /> Should be, ...the monsters in the deep that <b>he</b> mistook...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 11-05-2015, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T21:56:00-08:00","id":755826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=754209#post754209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Noel/le is genderfluid (hence &quot;femme presentation&quot; in &quot;Kinship&quot; on p.146 and the use of &quot;he&quot; pronouns for Noel in Hero).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid I don't follow. &quot;Noelle&quot; is the feminine version of the name, &quot;Noel&quot; is the masculine one. &quot;Kinship&quot; introduces the character as a female vampire, and follows her on a hunt where she pretends to be a prostitute, feeding on the johns.<br /> <br /> In &quot;Lair&quot; (p. 196), James, Robin, and Ben argue over whether it was wise to bring said vampire to their shared Lair. Again, the story refers to the character as &quot;Noelle&quot;, and a female.<br /> <br /> By Occam's Razor (or &quot;KISS&quot;), that means &quot;Noel&quot; (and the reference to &quot;he&quot; - good catch on that, by the way), is a mistake. Two out of the three are clearly talking about a female vampire who calls herself &quot;Noelle&quot;, and there's no suggestion in any of the three pieces implying that the vampire is transgendered or a cross-dresser. Plus, mixing up &quot;Noel&quot; and &quot;Noelle&quot; is an easy enough mistake to make (I'm related to one of each, and I've seen it happen over and over and over again).<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: And in &quot;Inheritance&quot;(p. 276), its back to &quot;Noelle&quot;, the female vampire. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 11-05-2015, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T22:05:59-08:00","id":755831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=755826#post755826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid I don't follow. &quot;Noelle&quot; is the feminine version of the name, &quot;Noel&quot; is the masculine one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Sometimes the vampire is a lady and sometimes the vampire is a man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Kinship&quot; introduces the character as a female vampire, and follows her on a hunt where she pretends to be a prostitute, feeding on the johns.<br /> <br /> In &quot;Lair&quot; (p. 196), James, Robin, and Ben argue over whether it was wise to bring said vampire to their shared Lair. Again, the story refers to the character as &quot;Noelle&quot;, and a female.<br /> <br /> [\u2026]<br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: And in &quot;Inheritance&quot;(p. 276), its back to &quot;Noelle&quot;, the female vampire. </div> </div> </div>And <u>back</u> in &quot;Kinship,&quot; we have the entire middle of the third paragraph:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cYou really want to do this?\u201d Noelle nodded her head toward the alley. If everything was going right, her \u201cdate\u201d would be waiting already. <b>It was so much easier when she hunted in her femme presentation, she\u2019d told him. As Noel it took more effort and sometimes required a supernatural nudge to draw in prey, but as Noelle all it took was a carefully worded Craigslist ad.</b> \u201cIt\u2019s OK if you don\u2019t want to.\u201d </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By Occam's Razor (or &quot;KISS&quot;), that means &quot;Noel&quot; (and the reference to &quot;he&quot; - good catch on that, by the way), is a mistake. Two out of the three are clearly talking about a female vampire who calls herself &quot;Noelle&quot;, and there's no suggestion in any of the three pieces implying that the vampire is transgendered or a cross-dresser. Plus, mixing up &quot;Noel&quot; and &quot;Noelle&quot; is an easy enough mistake to make (I'm related to one of each, and I've seen it happen over and over and over again). </div> </div> </div>See above. Also, one of my friends is (to repeat the word) <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genderqueer\" target=\"_blank\">genderfluid</a>. I'm reasonably certain that's precedent enough to identify &quot;sometimes they're a he and sometimes they're a she&quot; as not-a-mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-05-2015, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T22:47:05-08:00","id":755854,"title":"","content":"p.243<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Needless to say, this can result in retaliation from other broods, and so Beasts attempting to build their Legends this way often attempt to find allies first, sometimes by finding dreamers to Devour and sometimes by recruiting or subverting exist broods. Some would-be Incarnates, though, feel they are powerful enough to take on any challengers. Some of them are right. </div> </div> </div>Tense issue - pretty sure its supposed to be<br /> <br /> &quot;sometimes by recruiting or subverting exist<i><b>ing</b></i> broods.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Adopt the Beast-Shape:</b> The Begotten may physically transform into what her Horror reflects. She can call upon her Horror, letting it shift her body into a new, more powerful shape. </div> </div> </div>Maybe this is nitpicky, but this seems like an . . . overcomplicated way to say &quot;The Begotten shapeshifts into her Horror&quot;<br /> <br /> p. 244<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>No More Heroes</b>: Heroes might still seek the Beast out, but they cannot place Anathema on her and the Hero\u2019s power of Heroic Tracking is of no use. The Beast Incarnate can remove the Hero\u2019s gifts, granting him clarity and showing him exactly who he is in the scheme of things \u2014 an interloper, an intruder in a story that was never his. With a simple touch, the Beast shows the Hero that, no matter how terrifying the nightmare, it\u2019s not his place to end it. </div> </div> </div>Is there a system (or specific/practical consequences) to showing the Hero the truth?<br /> <br /> p.246<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Compounded by his nightly terror sprees through their dreams, however, he inevitably attracted Heroes, who decided to take matters into their own hands and slay the obvious monster in their midst. </div> </div> </div>&quot;however&quot; is a very awkward fit here. I suggest cutting it entirely.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T03:16:39-08:00","id":756149,"title":"","content":"pp. 17. the &quot;broods&quot; section. 2. paragraph, last sentence. &quot;Chambers in the<br /> area might on a bloody..&quot;. missing &quot;take&quot; -&gt; &quot;Chambers in the<br /> area might TAKE on a bloody..&quot;<br /> <br /> pp. 47, in the tanya tale. in the 3. to last paragraph.<br /> &quot;cold and eternal just like had been the night&quot; i think its missing an &quot;it&quot; -&gt; &quot;cold and eternal just like IT had been the night&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8728-sethe","name":"Sethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T09:34:15-08:00","id":756676,"title":"","content":"Page 87 Under Cautious<br /> &quot;do unto others before they do unto you, <b>such shooting</b> your enemy&quot;<br /> needs the word &quot;as&quot; in between<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5284-sanaelar","name":"Sanaelar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5284_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T18:13:05-08:00","id":757618,"title":"","content":"P. 85, under step seven. &quot;Mrs. Winters' Speed is 4 (Size) +...&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless the rules have changed, this should be &quot;Mrs. Winters' Speed is 5 (Species Factor) +...&quot;<br /> <br /> Also on p. 85, second paragraph under Legend. &quot;Your character...in order to scare, impress, convince him...&quot; There needs to be a linking conjunction between &quot;impress,&quot; and &quot;convince&quot;. Could use &quot;or&quot; or could use &quot;and&quot; but need to use one of them.<br /> <br /> P. 86, under Life, 4th paragraph. &quot;...the Beast rejects the notion that he should just act what...&quot; Should be &quot;...the Beast rejects the notion that he should just act as what...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 11-05-2015, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T01:20:17-08:00","id":758230,"title":"","content":"I'm about halfway through, and I'm noticing a lot of repetition. The same ideas, sentences, and phrases keep turning up over and over, sometimes even on the same page. If that's deliberate, that's one thing - but that's also something one can fall into by accident.<br /> <br /> For example, one of the more subtle examples involves the nightmare imagery. The giant, the tentacles pulling the subject into the water, the pursuit of a giant aerial predator . . . from the introduction to the back cover, those three keep coming up, over and over again. <br /> <br /> Now, as they're very iconic nightmare imagery, and are featured prominently in the Kickstarter pitch, I understand using a fair amount. But the three together, and neglecting other nightmare icons . . .<br /> <br /> <b>p. 251</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True, the edges have been nibbled away by strip centers and suburbs, . . . </div> </div> </div>Maybe this is a regional dialect issue, but &quot;strip centers&quot;? I'm familiar with &quot;strip malls&quot;, but have not encountered the phrase &quot;strip center&quot; before.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the whole &quot;Darkness in the Trees&quot; section is another example of (possible accidental) repetition. Is it really necessary to keep pointing out the pine trees, every two-three sentences?<br /> <br /> <b>p. 252</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A short drive from a number of major cities, the Pine Barrens could well draw any number of Beasts to poke around its isolate areas. </div> </div> </div>Possible typo - shouldn't that be &quot;isolate<b>d </b>areas&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She knows more about the Pine Barrens than any living creature, including the final resting place of a significant proportion of those who have gone missing in the Pines and lord knows what other tidbits picked up during a decades of riddling and strangling in the World of Darkness. </div> </div> </div>Two apparent typos. Isn't &quot;Lord&quot; (in &quot;lord knows&quot;) usually capitalized? And &quot;during a decades of riddling&quot; has an extra &quot;a&quot; - since Edna's been there for decades, it should probably read &quot;during decades of riddling&quot;.<br /> <br /> One concern, though. Edna's undergone the Merger. How does she have enough mind left to come up with riddles, or swap secrets? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> During the 18th and 19th centuries the Pine Barrens were a major center of American iron production, bog iron deposited by waters bubbling up from the depths of the earth. </div> </div> </div>Probably should be a comma after &quot;centuries&quot;. And shouldn't &quot;centuries&quot; be capitalized, since its a proper name (<i>a la</i> the Eighteenth Century, etc.)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (As a point of interest, World of Darkness: Urban Legends presents a different take on the Jersey Devil, but there\u2019s no reason that book\u2019s version and Edna couldn\u2019t co-exist.) </div> </div> </div>Given that its already pretty clear that Edna <i>isn't</i> the Jersey Devil, this line seems . . . redundant. Might want to consider switching it out for a cross-promotional one (&quot;For more secrets of the Pine Barrens, check out <i>Urban Legends today!&quot;)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T01:55:16-08:00","id":758292,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 289</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heroes can be difficult to use effectively because we tend to think of them as, well, heroes. They are called &quot;Heroes&quot; for reason, though (they could just as easily have been called &quot;Slayers,&quot; which would have conveyed a different message): Beast is about the monster/monster killer narrative, but it\u2019s meant to subvert it. Beasts aren\u2019t necessarily good people; they can be, but it\u2019s not a prerequisite for being the protagonist. Heroes aren\u2019t necessarily good people, either </div> </div> </div>There's a typo in the second sentence. It should be &quot;They are called &quot;Heroes&quot; for <b>a</b> reason&quot;. I'd also be tempted to make &quot;Beasts aren't necessarily good people&quot; its own sentence.<br /> <br /> However, in a very different direction, I'm also not wild about the &quot;Slayers&quot; line:<br /> <br /> &quot;they could just as easily have been called &quot;Slayers,&quot; which would have conveyed a different message&quot;<br /> <br /> Off-hand, I don't notice any grammar issues or typos. However, including it would seem to be in poor taste. The point about word choice influencing interpretation was made (often, loudly, and repeatedly) about the switch from &quot;Homecoming&quot; to &quot;Devouring&quot;, and &quot;Soul&quot; to &quot;Horror&quot; . . . and kind of blown off. Throwing it in here, about why the Heroes weren't renamed . . . kind of seems like trolling for a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T20:07:34-08:00","id":760440,"title":"","content":"P. 99 Inflicting Nightmares -- ...humans...who are in a deep state of consciousness...<br /> <br /> I think this is likely supposed to be ...a deep state of placidness...<br /> <br /> The use of consciousness is just weird and doesn't really agree with the examples in the following sentence.<br /> <br /> Also pp 94-95, Expanding the Lair: It isn't clear at all that the first bullet only applies to the next two and that the final bullet is an alternative to the three that precede it. Also not too clear that the chunk of rules really only applies to the final bullet. Presumably locations fulfilling any combination of the first three bullets allow the Beast to skip straight to paying Satiety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T14:05:30-08:00","id":760926,"title":"","content":"All the stray &quot;Soul&quot; and &quot;Homecoming&quot; references that haven't been caught yet (as far as I can see):<br /> <br /> <b>p. 29: </b>&quot;When a Lurker\u2019s <b>Soul </b>is unleashed...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 38:</b> &quot;...on the monstrous body of the Collector\u2019s <b>Soul</b>...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 248: </b>&quot;Ben felt his <b>Soul</b>\u2019s strength surge through him...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 294:</b> &quot;...when the character\u2019s <b>Soul </b>inflicts nightmares...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 294: </b>&quot;...when his <b>Soul </b>goes roaming in this area in the future...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 295:</b> &quot;...and the Beast\u2019s monstrous <b>Soul </b>builds a nest with the fragments...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 79: </b>&quot;At the moment of their <b>Homecoming</b>...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 80:</b> &quot;Once she has her <b>Homecoming</b>...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 80:</b> &quot;If her <b>Homecoming </b>was recent...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 248:</b> &quot;Nothing had really so much as scratched him since his <b>Homecoming</b>...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 337:</b> &quot;Once she has her <b>Homecoming</b>, she cannot deny the instinctual draw of her Lair, no matter what she does. If her <b>Homecoming </b>was recent, she still feels a draw to her human self, however, and might be less inclined or even reluctant to let her inner self out.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 