m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T16:09:00-08:00","id":761009,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 72:</b> &quot;(Don\u2019t become a monster, children.).&quot; That first period is probably extraneous?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-08-2015, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T21:02:26-08:00","id":761208,"title":"","content":"Can we add the number of nightmares and atavisms a beast is supposed to take by default to the quick reference? looking up this detail is painful. Changing p81 to this would be sufficient. (it is 2 and 2 right? trying to find the numbers outside of inference from example and having trouble)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Add Beast Template<br /> Choose Family, Hunger, Legend, Life, Kinship,<br /> Nightmares(2), Atavisms(2), and Lair. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 11-09-2015, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T21:22:38-08:00","id":761992,"title":"","content":"P. 105, under Corrosive -- &quot;...defines what the corrosion effects based on...&quot;<br /> <br /> Should be, &quot;...defines what the corrosion effects are based on...&quot;<br /> <br /> Pp. 106-7, presumably the major Lair traits are meant to be presented in alphabetical order; however, Suffocating appears before Razored and Rotting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 11-10-2015, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T21:36:59-08:00","id":761993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=761992#post761992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P. 105, under Corrosive -- &quot;...defines what the corrosion effects based on...&quot;<br /> <br /> Should be, &quot;...defines what the corrosion effects are based on...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026My copy has that line as <b>affects</b> and thus is perfectly fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T08:37:50-08:00","id":762342,"title":"","content":"Wait...did I misread...it was pretty late. <br /> <br /> Withdraw if the word is indeed <b>affects</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T15:42:05-08:00","id":762665,"title":"","content":"P. 108 -- Feeding: &quot;...until he's either completely ruins or...<br /> <br /> The phrasing seems odd. Perhaps it should be &quot;...until he's either completely ruin<b>ed</b> or...&quot; _or_ &quot;...until he's either completely <b>in a ruin</b> or...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 11-10-2015, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T20:31:17-08:00","id":762797,"title":"","content":"P. 115 -- Fist of Nightmares: Presumably one must also be a Beast in addition to the other prerequisites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T02:34:39-08:00","id":762953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/710646-beast-the-primordial-backer-pdf-errata-thread-it-s-out-now?p=755831#post755831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Sometimes the vampire is a lady and sometimes the vampire is a man.<br /> <br /> And <u>back</u> in &quot;Kinship,&quot; we have the entire middle of the third paragraph:</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm . . . you have a point - I totally missed the &quot;femme presentation&quot; bit.<br /> <br /> There's still an issue, though. Unless the vampires of <i>Requiem</i> have a gender swapping power (<i>a la</i> the kuei-jin of oWoD), the writers need to pick a gender for Ben's &quot;dinner date&quot;. Swapping pronouns back and forth (between &quot;he&quot; and &quot;she&quot;) is confusing. And said vampire's name is either &quot;Noel&quot;, or &quot;Noelle&quot;. Traditionally, the alternate persona has their name and gender written in quotes, to distinguish it. So the writers do need to commit, one way or the other.<br /> <br /> Given that Robin (the cat Beast) describes said vampire as female, after seeing Noel/Noelle walking around in rags, that's the direction I'd go in. Plus, that gives the work some degree of parity, seeing as Patrick and Ahmed (the other signature couple in the book) are gay.<br /> <br /> (I suppose another option would be to use the non-standard pronouns they used for the sample Beasts who refused to reveal their gender: &quot;zie&quot;, and so on. I'm not wild about the notion of using non-standard pronouns in general, but at least it would be consistent across the entire arc of Ben's story, then)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See above. Also, one of my friends is (to repeat the word) <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genderqueer\" target=\"_blank\">genderfluid</a>. I'm reasonably certain that's precedent enough to identify &quot;sometimes they're a he and sometimes they're a she&quot; as not-a-mistake. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#ff0000\">Please drop the gender topic. Thank you.<br /> <br /> -Pendragon</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-25-2015, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T03:17:34-08:00","id":762973,"title":"","content":"<b>Blood on the Border</b><br /> <br /> p.252<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ciudad Ju<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">\u00e1</span>rez, Mexico, is a city of industry with 1.5 million residents and hundreds of maquiladoras pumping out goods for the vast market of the United States just across the Rio Bravo (called Rio Grande by the gringos) </div> </div> </div>&quot;Maquiladoras&quot;? I'm all for conveying local color, and using the correct vocabulary, but &quot;maquiladoras&quot; is definitely not part of English yet. Either it needs to be defined in the text (like they did with Rio Bravo/Grande), or in a footnote.<br /> <br /> (Even after looking up the term, I'm not clear on whether they're &quot;legit&quot; factories, sweat shops, or something worse)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A city of dark mystery, with thousands disappeared and killed by unknown assailants. </div> </div> </div>While I've seen &quot;disappeared&quot; used to describe quietly killing someone, then hiding the body, it disrupts the flow here. Probably the best fix would be a rewrite, perhaps along the lines of<br /> <br /> &quot;A city of dark mystery, with thousands &quot;disappeared&quot; or outright killed by unknown assailants.&quot;<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> &quot;A city of dark mystery, where thousands disappear or are killed by unknown assailants.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A city of violence, temporarily quiescent as the government abandons its war on the cartels and the victors lick their wounds </div> </div> </div>Might want a comma after &quot;cartels&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ju<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">\u00e1</span>rez holds both promise and danger for Beasts as well. </div> </div> </div>Not wild about the &quot;as well&quot;. Switching back from italics provides a natural break in the flow of the text, rendering &quot;as well&quot; almost dangling. I suggest cutting it, or adding a subordinate clause at the beginning to provide a stronger connection to the last line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the one hand, it seems to offer a vast smorgasbord of opportunities to satisfy their Hungers with little chance of being caught. </div> </div> </div>I suggest dropping &quot;seems to&quot;, particularly since you're presenting this as the &quot;good&quot; side of relocating to the city, counterbalancing all the competition (and dangers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The city is rife with property crime, providing many opportunities for Collectors and the other Hungers </div> </div> </div>'Collectors&quot; and &quot;the other Hungers&quot; seem mismatched.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and a pair of twin Heroes are turning the tables on Beasts lured to the city. </div> </div> </div>This is nitpicky, but &quot;are turning&quot; is kind of passive, particularly for a threat. If you have a moment, consider going with something a bit more dynamic, <i>a la</i> &quot;twin Heroes already stalk the city&quot;, or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although the area around Ciudad Ju<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">\u00e1</span>rez has been inhabited for thousands of years by bands of hunter-gatherers and later by corn-growing agriculturalists, the history of the city itself began in 1659, when Mission Nuestra Se<span style=\"font-family:WP MultinationalA Roman\">\uf05a</span>ora de Guadalupe was established by the Franciscan order to proselytize to the local native population. </div> </div> </div>Borderline run-on sentence. You need a comma after &quot;hunter-gatherers&quot;, at least. And I strongly recommend breaking it into two sentences, with a period after &quot;1659&quot;. One option would be:<br /> <br /> &quot;Although the area around Ciudad Ju<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">\u00e1</span>rez has been inhabited for thousands of years by bands of hunter-gatherers, and later by corn-growing agriculturalists, the history of the city itself began in 1659. That year, Franciscan monks established Mission Nuestra Se<span style=\"font-family:WP MultinationalA Roman\">\uf05a</span>ora de Guadalupe to proselytize to the local native population.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aside from a few ambiguous petroglyphs, the first evidence of Beasts in Paso del Norte as Ju<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">\u00e1</span>rez was then known dates from this era. A written account of a Spanish brood headed toward Santa Fe to investigate reports of vampires among the Pueblo peoples mentions passing through the town in 1678. The Pueblo Revolt of 1680 then sent colonial and pro-Spanish Indian refugees flooding into the outpost. </div> </div> </div>As the supernatural history of the area, this should probably be its own paragraph, rather than fused with the early (mundane) history.<br /> <br /> Also not wild about the &quot;headed toward Santa Fe to investigate reports of vampires among the Pueblo peoples &quot; bit. Its an interesting tidbit, but its almost a separate thought shoehorned into the sentence. Consider cutting it, or using parenthesis or hyphens to set it off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Paso del Norte passed through the Mexican War of Independence of the early 19th century relatively unscathed, but shifts in the river had a lasting impact, putting several local communities on the north side of the Rio Bravo\u2019s new course. </div> </div> </div>Not wild about &quot;of the early 19th century&quot;. First, &quot;century&quot; should be capitalized. Second . . . it makes it sound like there have been multiple Mexican Wars of Independence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Texas Revolution too had little effect on Ju<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">\u00e1</span>rez, despite the new Republic\u2019s claim of the Rio Bravo as its southern border. </div> </div> </div>Need commas around &quot;too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 11-11-2015, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T08:07:24-08:00","id":763120,"title":"","content":"Thanks, everyone!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}